ACTION REQUIRED — replace this file with the full licence text
================================================================================

This file currently contains only the copyright notice. A valid GPL-3.0
distribution must include the COMPLETE licence text (~675 lines).

Get it in either of these ways:

  1. Download it directly:
         https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt
     Save it as LICENSE, then paste the copyright notice above at the very top.

  2. Let GitHub do it for you (easiest):
     In your repository, click "Add file" -> "Create new file", name the file
     LICENSE, and GitHub will offer a "Choose a license template" button.
     Pick "GNU General Public License v3.0", fill in the year (2026) and your
     name (Benjamin Klugah-Brown), and commit. GitHub inserts the full official
     text for you.

Option 2 is recommended: it guarantees the text is correct and unmodified, and
GitHub will then display the licence badge on your repository page.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note on third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MBCT integrates and depends upon external toolboxes and reference datasets that
are NOT covered by this licence and retain their own terms:

  * cbig_network_correspondence (Network Correspondence Toolbox, CBIG)
  * NiMARE / Neurosynth
  * neuromaps and the PET receptor atlas of Hansen et al. (2022)
  * abagen and the Allen Human Brain Atlas
  * BrainSMASH
  * FSL atlases (Harvard-Oxford, JHU-ICBM)
  * MNI152 templates
  * PyQt6, nibabel, nilearn, NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib, pandas, statsmodels

Users and redistributors are responsible for complying with the licences and
data-use agreements of these components. Note in particular that PyQt6 is
distributed under the GPL (or a commercial licence from Riverbank Computing);
distributing MBCT under the GPL-3.0 is consistent with PyQt6's GPL terms.
